# Sync Config

## Calendar ID

> Your Google Calendar ID. Find it in Google Calendar → Settings → your calendar → "Calendar ID".
> Example: `yourname@gmail.com` or `abc123xyz@group.calendar.google.com`

{{CALENDAR_ID}}

## API Key

> Optional but recommended for personal calendars. A Google Cloud API key with the Calendar API enabled.
> Create one at console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create API key.
> Enable "Google Calendar API" for the project. No OAuth or browser flow required.
> Leave blank to fall back to ICS (public calendars only) or MCP.

{{API_KEY}}

## Public Source

> Optional. An additional read-only sync source — a public Google Calendar ID or a public ICS URL.
> Public GCals (e.g. holidays, sports seasons) are fetched via `list_events` with no extra OAuth.
> ICS URLs are fetched and parsed directly. Leave blank or keep the placeholder to disable.
> Public events are marked read-only in cards; use `send-to-gcal` to copy one to your own calendar.
> Example (US holidays): `en.usa#holiday@group.v.calendar.google.com`

{{PUBLIC_SOURCE}}

## Sync Range

> Default range used by `calendardeck-sync` when no explicit range is given.
> Examples: `current-month`, `next-30-days`, `2026-06-01–2026-06-30`

{{SYNC_RANGE}}

